WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.200
Rhiannon: Puberty can be a challenging
time as hormones kick in and children

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.630
develop new moods and feelings
and the "emotional rollercoaster"

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:11.959
they're on, can have real lasting
psychological effects, The physical

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:16.200
changes give rise to a variety of
social and emotional changes as well,

00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:18.670
directly affecting the body and brain.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:22.680
They start to look and act
differently, and an array of social

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.529
influences further accelerate
these social and emotional changes.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.689
Leah: As their bodies change, they
may experience a new and unfamiliar

00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:35.209
set of social experiences and become
interested in forming what can become

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.790
intense, romantic, and sometimes
sexualised relationships with others

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.070
and they may be start to become
treated by society differently.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.669
Those who mature quickly may be more
popular than those who mature slowly.

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:50.920
Adults may also view them differently
expecting more adult behaviour, when

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.539
they are still more or less a child.

00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:56.050
Rhiannon: Body dissatisfaction
has been linked to depression and

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:00.510
anxiety particularly in children
who do not match the ‘ideal body’.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:05.670
Young people who are overweight can have
lower self-esteem than their peers and may

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:11.359
look to weight control options, such as
using diet pills, diuretics and laxatives.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:16.590
Leah: Children and young people with poor
body image are less likely to take part

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:20.980
in physical activities due to worries
about their appearance, this can therefore

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.859
compound their possible health issues.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:27.119
Whilst those with good body image are
less likely to diet or use alcohol or

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.340
cigarettes, increasing the chance of more
positive mental health and well-being.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.460
Rhiannon: While body image concerns
affect both boys and girls, more girls

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.959
are likely to be dissatisfied with
their appearance and their weight

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:44.530
and more likely to consider going on
a diet or having cosmetic surgery.

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:48.530
Whereas boys are less likely but
might be more inclined to look

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.260
at using steroids to bulk up.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:54.270
These behaviours can be the start
of further mental health problems.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.960
Leah: Young women often report feeling
a pressure to be thin, but to still

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.139
maintain curves, especially when they
see how ‘the ideal’ is portrayed on

00:02:03.139 --> 00:02:07.669
social media, therefore they may look to
having procedures to enhance themselves.

00:02:08.389 --> 00:02:11.810
Young men often report pressure to
be tall and more muscular so may hit

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:16.060
the gym, start lifting wights and
bulking up naturally or using steroids.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:20.490
Rhiannon: How young people develop their
sense of ‘ideal’ appearance is varied.

00:02:20.889 --> 00:02:24.590
Young people themselves identify
the media, pressure from family and

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:28.480
friends, comparisons with peers,
and personal factors like low

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.790
self-esteem, feelings of depression,
and a need for control, as important

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:34.810
influences on their own body image.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:39.359
We need to be mindful of all of these
factors to potentially counter some of

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:43.650
the negative affects they can have on
children and young people’s mental health.

